# Repository-owned gitleaks false-positive ledger. Mechanism sanctioned by
# .gitleaks.toml ("Intentional findings use a repository-owned .gitleaksignore
# or inline `gitleaks:allow` comment"). One fingerprint per line:
# <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<start-line>.
#
# Both entries below are the generic-api-key rule keying on the identifier in
# `CLAUDE_TOKEN=""` (an empty parser-state variable) and capturing the integer
# flag `CLAUDE_SHIM=0` on the next line as its "secret". Nothing is disclosed;
# full diagnosis and reproduction live in issue #3599. The commits sit on other
# in-flight branches, but CI's `scan-mode: git` walks every ref in the clone,
# so they fail hygiene on every pull request until ignored here or until those
# refs stop carrying the unannotated commits. Each entry goes stale (and can be
# deleted) once its commit is no longer reachable from any ref.
